# Placeholder for GoogleService-Info.plist

This file should be downloaded from your Firebase Console after setting up your iOS app.

## How to get this file:

1. Go to [Firebase Console](https://console.firebase.google.com/)
2. Select your project
3. Click on the iOS icon or go to Project Settings
4. Under "Your apps", find your iOS app
5. Click "Download GoogleService-Info.plist"
6. Replace this file with the downloaded `GoogleService-Info.plist`
7. Add the file to your Xcode project (drag into Runner folder in Xcode)

## Important:
- This file contains your Firebase configuration for iOS
- Do NOT commit the actual `GoogleService-Info.plist` to version control if it contains sensitive data
- Add `GoogleService-Info.plist` to your `.gitignore` if needed
- You must also configure APNs (Apple Push Notification service) in Firebase Console

For detailed instructions, see: `firebase_setup_guide.md`
